From 6b43497330399bfc8711289a3e873868a8af910f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:14:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: visit the Borg's own grid in the call-light scan

The call-light scan in borg_think_dungeon_light() iterated the eight
neighbours only (ii < 8), but its open/broken-door case tests the
Borg's own grid (y == borg.c.y && x == borg.c.x) -- a case that could
never fire, so the is-the-door-lit cheat (square_isglow) never ran and
an open doorway underfoot kept whatever glow mark the Borg's map
happened to hold. Include index 8 (the Borg's own grid, ddx_ddd[8] ==
ddy_ddd[8] == 0) so the door case runs, and so a dark own grid can be
lit by the routine like any other grid.
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index bdc8e1a32..e4687edc6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -253,8 +253,9 @@ bool borg_think_dungeon_light(void)
          */
         if (borg.time.call_light == 0
             || (borg_timer(borg.time.call_light) > 7)) {
-            /* Scan grids adjacent to me */
-            for (ii = 0; ii < 8; ii++) {
+            /* Scan the grids adjacent to me and my own grid (an open
+             * door underfoot is handled below) */
+            for (ii = 0; ii <= 8; ii++) {
                 x = borg.c.x + ddx_ddd[ii];
                 y = borg.c.y + ddy_ddd[ii];
 
